'''Buttons''', originally cut content in ''[[The Binding of Isaac: Rebirth]]'', have become a full-fledged feature of ''[[The Binding of Isaac: Afterbirth]]''.

== Pressure Plate ==
{{infobox entity
 | hidden = yes
 | name   = Pressure Plate
}}
[[file:Pressure Plate.png|50px]]

'''Pressure Plates''' appear in trap rooms, which have [[obstacle|hazards]] in them which disarm upon pressing all of the plates in the room. Hazards include:
* [[Spikes]]
* [[Retractable Spikes]]
* {{E|TNT}}
* {{e|Troll Bomb}}s
* {{e|Mega Troll Bomb}}s
* {{E|Stone Grimace}}s
* {{E|Vomit Grimace}}s
* {{E|Constant Stone Shooter}}s
* {{E|Gaping Maw}}s
* {{E|Broken Gaping Maw}}s
* {{E|Brimstone Head}}s
* {{E|Cross Stone Shooter}}s
* {{E|Quake Grimace}}s
* {{E|Poky|text=Pokies}}
* {{E|Wall Hugger}}s
* {{E|Slide}}s
* {{E|Grudge}}s
* {{E|Spikeball}}s
* {{E|Red Poop}}
* {{E|Red Fire Place}}s
* {{E|Purple Fire Place}}s
* {{E|Pitfall}}s
Once pressed, all the hazards will be disarmed — spikes will retract, Red Poop will transform into regular Poop, Red Fire Places will turn into regular Fire Places, Purple Fire Places will turn into Blue Fire Places, and Pitfalls will close.
{{clear}}
Unlike Reward Plates, all Pressure Plates in the room have to be pressed to clear the room, even if all enemies are slain.

{{bug|In trap rooms with retracting spikes, pressing the plate within five frames of the spikes deploying will cause them to appear to fail to retract, but this is only a visual bug, and they will not deal damage. This can be fixed by leaving the room and re-entering.}}

== Kill Plate (Killswitch) {{dlc+|r}} ==
{{infobox entity
 | hidden = yes
 | name   = Killswitch
 | dlc    = r
}}
[[File:Killswitch.png|50px]]

'''Kill Plates''' usually appear in normal rooms.

Once pressed, all enemies will be killed and all enemy projectiles will be destroyed. Enemies that normally spawn another enemy or shoot projectiles upon death will not do so if slain by a Kill Plate. Kill Plates also disarm all the same hazards that Pressure Plates can, but unlike said buttons, they don't need to be pressed to clear a room. Kill Plates can also uncover the hidden crawl space in the {{e|Great Gideon}} boss fight.

Kill Plates often appear either hidden behind tall blocks or in rooms filled with enemies either too great in numbers to fight off normally or that are blocked from the player's attacks, therefore requiring the button to clear the room.
{{dlc-}}

== Rail Plate {{dlc+|r}} ==
{{infobox entity
 | hidden = yes
 | name   = Yellow Button
 | dlc    = r
}}
[[File:Yellow Button.png|50px]]

'''Rail Plates''' only appear in the second {{s|Mines}} or {{s|Ashpit}} floor if Isaac has acquired {{i|Knife Piece 1}}, and are square-shaped.

Pressing all 3 yellow buttons throughout the floor unlocks the bridge to {{i|Knife Piece 2}}.

Rail Plates may appear in {{R|Red Room}}s, in which case they will not do anything.
{{dlc-}}

== Event Plate {{dlc+|r}} ==
{{infobox entity
 | hidden = yes
 | name   = Brown Button
 | dlc    = r
}}
[[File:Brown Button.png|50px]]

'''Event Plates''' cause certain pits (varies from room to room) to be filled so they can be walked on. Sometimes it clears rocks instead. Event Plates are also capable of spawning enemies, pickups, and items or deactivating or reactivating teleporters, which all vary from room to room as well. Event Plates are most commonly found in the alternative path such as {{S|Mines}} and {{S|Mausoleum}}, where they may sometimes be hidden behind tall blocks, which often grant access to rewards in the room that are otherwise inaccessible.
{{dlc-}}

== Reward Plate ==
{{infobox entity
 | hidden = yes
 | name   = Reward Plate
}}
[[file:Reward Plate.png|50px]]

'''Reward Plates''' can appear in a variety of rooms, including {{R|Secret Room}}s, {{R|Curse Room}}s, and {{R|Shop}}s in [[Greed mode]]. When pressed, they may spawn helpful pickups or harmful enemies. Reward Plates differ from an Event Plate's ability to spawn pickups and enemies by the fact that it is completely random every time as opposed to Event Plates having a preset spawn for the specific room it is in.

=== Possible Spawns ===
